{"4550080": {"success": true, "data": {"type": "game", "name": "Super Gerio Town", "steam_appid": 4550080, "required_age": 0, "is_free": false, "controller_support": "full", "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Game Overview]</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>A new‑style indie action game that blends classic retro gameplay with the realism of human bodily needs</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Game Description]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >On his way home, the weak‑stomached Gerio must dodge obstacles and rush into toilets whenever he can.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will he make it back home without an accident? <strong>The outcome is up to you!</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Objective]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avoid Splashing as much as possible, reach the toilet in each stage, and guide Gerio safely back home!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Game System]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The first thing you’ll notice is a mysterious gauge called the “DiarrMeter.”</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If this meter fills up… “Splash!”</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jumping or taking damage increases the meter, while crouching lowers it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple controls, but balancing action and meter management is the key to success.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Main Gameplay Elements</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Manage the DiarrMeter</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Jumping or enemy attacks raise the meter</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Crouching or collecting apples lowers it</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Entering a toilet completely resets it (refreshing!)</strong></p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If it fills up… Splash!</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Avoid various enemies</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Getting hit increases the meter</strong></p></li></ul></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Story]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gerio once again feels trouble brewing in his stomach on his way home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avoid Splashing, rush into toilets, and help him make it back safely.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Features]</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Retro‑style side‑scrolling action</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cute and colorful pixel‑art graphics</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A unique experience that’s both funny and a little stressful</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Difficulty increases as you progress</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Additional Information]</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Playtime: About 1–20 minutes per stage</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Difficulty: Starts beginner‑friendly and gradually becomes more challenging</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Graphics: Pop and colorful pixel art</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sound: Upbeat, retro‑inspired music</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Total Stages: 20</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Genre]</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Retro</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pop</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Action Game</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Side‑Scrolling Action</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pixel Art</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Additional Game Modes / Character Progression]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >None</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Lastly]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rumor has it… there might be a certain item that can help Gerio prevent a Splash. Or maybe not.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[About the Use of AI]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game uses AI tools only to help create some of the music and chord patterns.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All gameplay systems, level design, controls, and game mechanics were designed by the developer. <br>AI was used only to assist in converting these ideas into assets or code.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >AI does not influence gameplay in any way and is used solely as a support tool during asset creation.</p>", "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Game Overview]</strong></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>A new‑style indie action game that blends classic retro gameplay with the realism of human bodily needs</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Game Description]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >On his way home, the weak‑stomached Gerio must dodge obstacles and rush into toilets whenever he can.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Will he make it back home without an accident? <strong>The outcome is up to you!</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Objective]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avoid Splashing as much as possible, reach the toilet in each stage, and guide Gerio safely back home!</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Game System]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The first thing you’ll notice is a mysterious gauge called the “DiarrMeter.”</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If this meter fills up… “Splash!”</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Jumping or taking damage increases the meter, while crouching lowers it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Simple controls, but balancing action and meter management is the key to success.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Main Gameplay Elements</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Manage the DiarrMeter</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Jumping or enemy attacks raise the meter</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Crouching or collecting apples lowers it</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Entering a toilet completely resets it (refreshing!)</strong></p></li></ul></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>If it fills up… Splash!</strong></p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Avoid various enemies</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Getting hit increases the meter</strong></p></li></ul></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Story]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Gerio once again feels trouble brewing in his stomach on his way home.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Avoid Splashing, rush into toilets, and help him make it back safely.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Features]</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Retro‑style side‑scrolling action</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Cute and colorful pixel‑art graphics</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A unique experience that’s both funny and a little stressful</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Difficulty increases as you progress</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Additional Information]</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Playtime: About 1–20 minutes per stage</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Difficulty: Starts beginner‑friendly and gradually becomes more challenging</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Graphics: Pop and colorful pixel art</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Sound: Upbeat, retro‑inspired music</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Total Stages: 20</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Genre]</strong></p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Retro</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pop</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Action Game</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Side‑Scrolling Action</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pixel Art</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Additional Game Modes / Character Progression]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >None</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[Lastly]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Rumor has it… there might be a certain item that can help Gerio prevent a Splash. Or maybe not.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>[About the Use of AI]</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This game uses AI tools only to help create some of the music and chord patterns.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >All gameplay systems, level design, controls, and game mechanics were designed by the developer. <br>AI was used only to assist in converting these ideas into assets or code.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >AI does not influence gameplay in any way and is used solely as a support tool during asset creation.</p>", "short_description": "A new‑style indie action game that blends classic retro gameplay with the realism of human bodily needs. “Will you make it… or will you burst?”", "supported_languages": "English, Japanese", "header_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4550080/e166920a0ed3a75573582af839368d8380dbe269/header.jpg?t=1775805012", "capsule_image": "https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4550080/c00ac8689dc5